id=scr01_sms_enable
name=SCR-01 SMS Enable
version=2.2
versionCode=4
author=Toko + Deepseek Harness
description=Enables SMS send+receive on the Samsung SCR-01 (data-only 5G router) by making config_sms_capable visible to the framework via a cinnamon theme overlay, forcing the android.app.role.SMS role into the available-role list, and granting it to a configurable default SMS app (Fossify Messages). v2.2 adds a built-in APN database generated from LineageOS android_vendor_apn (Apache-2.0), inserts the missing default/IMS APNs for both the SIM PLMN and the registered PLMN, patches the active Samsung IMS profile (support_roaming, smsip, ipver=ipv4v6, enc_algo=all), rotates its log (128 KiB + one backup), and ships collect-logs.sh for troubleshooting. Mobile data / roaming data can stay OFF: Samsung's always-on IMS PDN still carries SMS (verified with Skinny NZ 53005 roaming on China Mobile 46000). Reversible via uninstall.sh; no real partition is written.
